---
import Site from '../layouts/Site.astro';
import ClaimBlock from '../components/ClaimBlock.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import { release, url } from '../lib/publication';
const funds = release.claims.find(c => c.id === 'C-JJM-FUNDS-20260331');
const karnataka = release.claims.find(c => c.id === 'C-KA-DROUGHT-ORDER-20260922');
---
<Site title="What government is doing" description="An evidence-stage account of documented water-programme action and the local response questions still open.">
  <PageHeader title="A promise, a payment, a result" eyebrow="Public response" description="Government action has stages. A release documents what an institution says it has done; service outcomes require another kind of evidence." />
  <section class="section"><div class="shell page-grid"><article>
    <p class="eyebrow">The documented national step</p><h2>Jal Jeevan Mission 2.0: approval and reported release</h2><p>In a <a href={funds ? url(`/sources/${funds.evidenceIds[0]}/`) : url('/sources/')}>31 March 2026 Ministry of Jal Shakti release</a>, the ministry said the Union Cabinet approved the programme on 10 March, guidelines followed on 22 March, and ₹1,561.53 crore was released to five named states for FY 2025–26. This is a reported programme step, <strong>not</strong> a verified September drought response, state expenditure, completed scheme or improved household service.</p>
    {karnataka && <div class="story-rail"><p class="eyebrow">Documented local action · Karnataka · 22 September 2026</p><h2>A declaration for 53 listed taluks</h2><p>A <a href={url(`/sources/${karnataka.evidenceIds[0]}/`)}>gazetted Revenue Department order</a> declared <strong>53 additional taluks in 17 districts</strong> drought-affected for the 2026 kharif season: 51 severe and two moderate. Effective immediately for up to six months unless revoked, it authorizes district authorities to undertake relief under SDRF norms and directs a joint crop-loss survey. The earlier orders it cites were not separately checked here, so this is not a statewide cumulative count. The declaration does not establish that relief reached anyone or that crop loss was measured.</p><a href={url('/states/karnataka/')}>Karnataka evidence page ↗</a></div>}
    <div class="figure"><p class="eyebrow">Action-stage ledger</p><div class="table-wrap"><table class="data-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Stage</th><th scope="col">What is verified here</th><th scope="col">What remains to establish</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Authority & announcement</td><td>Ministry-reported JJM Cabinet approval and guideline dates; Karnataka's 22 September gazetted drought declaration for 53 listed taluks.</td><td>Other place-specific orders and scope.</td></tr><tr><td>Money released</td><td>Ministry-reported FY 2025–26 JJM release of ₹1,561.53 crore to five named states.</td><td>Independent treasury record, allocation and later expenditure. The Karnataka order authorizes relief; it does not record delivery.</td></tr><tr><td>Implementation</td><td>No approved place-specific delivery finding.</td><td>Work and relief records, completion dates and service area.</td></tr><tr><td>Outcome</td><td>No approved crop-loss or service finding.</td><td>Joint survey result, relief received, and reliable quantity, quality and continuity measured for households.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class="small">The ministry release and Karnataka gazette are separate source chains. The stage table is a reading guide, not a scorecard.</p></div>
    <h2>What should be checked locally?</h2><p>A response to a specific shortage needs its own paper trail: who has authority for the source and service area; whether a contingency plan or order was issued; what money or water was allocated; when work happened; and what residents actually received. Beyond Karnataka's documented declaration, this release has no verified state or district delivery outcome. An absent record here does not show that an authority did nothing.</p>
    <div class="note"><strong>What might government do?</strong><p>Existing institutions can issue plans and advisories, manage sources and support delivery, but the relevant powers and current instructions vary by place. We will describe a mechanism as operative only when its current source is checked. No particular politician's future action is predicted here.</p></div>
  </article><aside><p class="eyebrow">Follow the documents</p><a href={url('/journalists/')}>Questions and records to request</a><a href={url('/what-you-can-do/')}>Find official local information</a><a href={url('/data-status/')}>Response coverage</a></aside></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="shell reading"><p class="eyebrow">Source-linked records</p>{karnataka && <ClaimBlock claim={karnataka} heading="Karnataka gazetted declaration, 22 September" />}{funds && <ClaimBlock claim={funds} heading="Ministry-reported 2026 programme step" />}</div></section>
</Site>
